tools/oracle licensing notice
=============================

The patch files in this directory are NOT under the repository's license. They are separate works,
distributed alongside this repository (mere aggregation, in the GPL's words) and never linked into,
compiled into or copied into the port.

patches/opengmk/*.patch
    Modifications to OpenGMK (https://github.com/OpenGMK/OpenGMK), Copyright (c) the OpenGMK
    contributors. OpenGMK is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 only
    (SPDX: GPL-2.0-only), and so are these patch files. The license text is in
    patches/opengmk/COPYING.md (a copy of OpenGMK's LICENCE.md). tools/oracle/build applies them to
    an unmodified checkout of OpenGMK at the commit pinned in tools/oracle/common.sh.

patches/ramen/*.patch
    Modifications to ramen (https://github.com/viriuwu/ramen), which OpenGMK uses for windowing.
    ramen is licensed under the zlib license, and so are these patch files. The license text is in
    patches/ramen/LICENCE.org (a copy of ramen's). As that license requires, the altered source is
    marked as such: these patches are not the original ramen.

These patches are the one deliberate exception to the rule in CLAUDE.md that OpenGMK code is never
copied into this repository: they exist only to build the oracle. Nothing else in the repository may
copy from them, and the port (crates/) must not use them as a source.

Everything else in tools/oracle (the scripts, Dockerfile, README and examples) is part of this
repository and contains no OpenGMK code. Neither the Spelunky User License (../../LICENSE) nor any
other license of this repository applies to the patch files, and the GPL does not extend to the rest
of the repository.
